# Computational benchmark and execution plan

All total times are extrapolations. Queue wait is excluded. A short benchmark does not establish model quality.

| Stage | Priority | Hardware | Measured speed/memory | Estimated total time | Proceed/fallback condition |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| pooled_gru training | Required | NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090 | 2877.2 spectra/s; 0.05 GiB allocated; 0.08 GiB at full caps (passed) | 2.43 h estimated | Commit as the reference; retain metrics on the same split |
| transformer training | Required | NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090 | 973.0 spectra/s; 0.86 GiB allocated; 1.16 GiB at full caps (passed) | 7.16 h estimated | Commit to this single Transformer if the base plan fits the budget; verify held-out MRR@25 |
| Beam decoding | Required | NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090 | 47.82 spectra/s; 0.28 GiB allocated; beam 25 | 0.01 h estimated for 553 validation + 1213 test spectra | Remeasure on validated weights; lower beam width or inference batch if needed |
| Ranker candidate generation | Optional | NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090 | 6.86 spectra/s; 100 samples/spectrum | 0.40 GPU h + 0.14 CPU h estimated | Only if candidate recall is useful and held-out ranker MRR@25 improves; remeasure with trained weights |
| Ranker fitting + refit | Optional | CPU, one thread | 58.8 s synthetic proxy; 1000000 candidate rows | 0.016 CPU h proxy | Replace proxy with real candidate fit; require validation gain |
| Ensemble | Deferred | NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090 | Unmeasured | Unestimated; no extra model committed | If estimated additional cost exceeds remaining budget, retain the single Transformer; otherwise require held-out MRR@25 gain |

Training uses 2,242,315 length-filtered spectra × 10 planned epochs. Formula: spectra × epochs / measured spectra/s / 3600, plus measured validation and checkpoint costs, 10% extra loading allowance, and preparation time. Steady-state data loading is already timed.

Training validation overhead measures teacher-forced token loss. The beam row budgets one structure-level evaluation on the prepared validation subset plus final test decoding; additional beam evaluations cost extra.

The baseline is a pooled peak-embedding encoder with a GRU decoder (128 dimensions, two GRU layers by default). Both models use the same train-only tokenizer, partitions, metadata and peak preprocessing. The Transformer uses the exact settings recorded in transformer.json. Full-cap memory is a separate stress test.

CPU ranker timing uses synthetic labels only; it provides no evidence of recall, ranking quality or validation gain. Decoding speed is conditional on beam width, generated lengths and benchmark weights. Remeasure on the first validated checkpoint.

No ranker or ensemble is committed until the budget is specified and held-out quality supports it. **If the estimated additional cost exceeds the remaining budget, retain the single Transformer.**

Total GPU-hour budget is still unspecified; optional stages remain deferred.
